    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The name Waldport comes from the German word for forest, combined with port, reflecting the town's coastal and wooded location.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waldport%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Non-Native settlement in Waldport began in 1879 after David Ruble purchased land rights for three hundred dollars.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waldport%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Waldport's early economy centered on salmon canneries, sawmills, dairying, and logging for over a century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waldport%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Conscientious objectors at a World War Two camp south of Waldport founded Untide Press to publish poetry and artwork.",
